From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: hid: answer feature reports with their byte count, advertise gyro caps

The host treats a feature-report reply's result as hid_get_feature_report's
return value: the number of bytes read, where anything <= 0 is a failure.
ihslib answered a successful read with result=0, so the host discarded every
feature report - the 0x04 caps report in particular, retried five times per
pad ("couldn't get controller details for SDL controller" in the host's
controller.txt, ~800 ms each) - and fell back to the CHIDDeviceInfo caps.
Reply with the byte count, as Valve's own client does.

Those fallback caps also lacked the gyro/accelerometer bits (0x00040800),
which Valve's client sets whenever SDL reports a gyro; without them Steam
Input offers no gyro settings at all for a streamed controller. Add them.

--- a/src/session/channels/control/control_hid.c
+++ b/src/session/channels/control/control_hid.c
@@ -398,8 +398,12 @@ static void HandleDeviceGetFeatureReport(IHS_SessionChannel *channel, IHS_HIDMan
 
     CHIDMessageFromRemote__RequestResponse response = CHIDMESSAGE_FROM_REMOTE__REQUEST_RESPONSE__INIT;
     PROTOBUF_C_SET_VALUE(response, request_id, message->request_id);
-    PROTOBUF_C_SET_VALUE(response, result, result);
-    if (result == 0) {
+    /* The host reads the result as hid_get_feature_report's return value: the
+     * number of bytes, and anything <= 0 is a failure. Valve's client answers
+     * with the byte count; a bare 0 made the host discard every feature report
+     * (caps, serial) and fall back to the generic caps below. */
+    PROTOBUF_C_SET_VALUE(response, result, result < 0 ? result : (int) str.size);
+    if (result >= 0) {
         response.has_data = true;
         response.data.data = IHS_BufferPointer(&str);
         response.data.len = str.size;
@@ -585,5 +589,9 @@ static void InfoFromHID(CHIDDeviceInfo *info, const IHS_HIDDeviceInfo *hid) {
                                  IHS_HID_CAP_STICKBTNS | IHS_HID_CAP_SHOULDERS | IHS_HID_CAP_TRIGGERS |
                                  IHS_HID_CAP_BACK | IHS_HID_CAP_START | IHS_HID_CAP_GUIDE | IHS_HID_CAP_MISC_1 |
                                  IHS_HID_CAP_XINPUT_OR_HIDAPI | IHS_HID_CAP_UNK_3 | IHS_HID_CAP_UNK_4;
+    /* Gyro + accelerometer (0x00040800, the bits Valve's client sets when SDL reports a
+     * gyro). The host only reads these caps when the 0x04 caps feature report fails, so
+     * this is the fallback that still lets Steam Input offer gyro. */
+    capsBits |= IHS_HID_CAP_UNK_1 | IHS_HID_CAP_UNK_5;
     PROTOBUF_C_P_SET_VALUE(info, caps_bits, capsBits);
 }
